--TEST--
A test the declared type already answers compiles and answers it, in both directions, and so does one written inside a branch that has already narrowed its subject — `rule:types/type-test`, `rule:types/narrowing`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/type-test` is total: nothing is refused for having a knowable
// answer. `int $n; $n is int` is `true` and `$n is string` is `false`, and
// neither is a diagnostic — that is the whole of what this case pins, so it
// is a case rather than a unit test: what is frozen is the answer a program
// gets, not which pass settled it.
//
// The neighbouring operator does refuse a subject of this shape
// (`rule:php-migration/a-declared-type-answers-before-the-program-runs`),
// because `instanceof` needs a class to test against and a scalar has none.
// `is` is applicable everywhere, every value having a representation, so a
// knowable answer here is not a meaningless question.

class Show {
    public static function yn(bool $b): string {
        if ($b) {
            return "y";
        }
        return "n";
    }
}

int $n = 7;
echo "int-is-int=", Show::yn($n is int), "\n";
echo "int-is-string=", Show::yn($n is string), "\n";

string $s = "ab";
echo "string-is-string=", Show::yn($s is string), "\n";
echo "string-is-int=", Show::yn($s is int), "\n";

// A declaration that fixes the type to one a value can hold with `null`
// beside it settles neither half by itself, and both spellings still read as
// the same operator.
?int $maybe = null;
echo "nullable-is-null=", Show::yn($maybe is null), "\n";
echo "nullable-is-int=", Show::yn($maybe is int), "\n";

// `rule:types/narrowing`: the second reason nothing is refused here. Inside
// the branch the guard proved, the subject is already an `int`, so the inner
// test is statically true by construction — refusing it would let a flow
// analysis turn working code into a compile error.
mixed $m = 42;
if ($m is int) {
    echo "narrowed-again=", Show::yn($m is int), "\n";
    echo "narrowed-is-string=", Show::yn($m is string), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
int-is-int=y
int-is-string=n
string-is-string=y
string-is-int=n
nullable-is-null=y
nullable-is-int=n
narrowed-again=y
narrowed-is-string=n
